You will be responsible for the following projects:
You will design schematic diagrams and printed circuit boards (PCBs) using Altium Designer;
You will contribute to the development and improvement of new versions of smart meters from a hardware perspective;
You will work with ultrasonic measurement solutions and products with low current consumption (at the μA level);
You will design and improve production line testing equipment;
You will identify and resolve emerging issues;
You will collaborate with specialists from the RnD and manufacturing departments.
We offer a hybrid work model (2 days per week from home).
Why is it good to be a member of our team?
We believe in our values: #I care, #I trust, #I create value for the client;
We are active in the global market of water and heat meters;
We have additional benefits for employees (annual bonuses, health insurance, training and learning budget, major annual events, gifts for various occasions, a day off on your birthday, rest areas with coffee and games);
We have the hybrid work model and the Workation option, i.e. we can work from abroad (up to 3 months);
Further career opportunities depend only on ourselves. Every 10th employee makes an internal career during the year;
Each of us has the freedom to contribute to the improvement of processes, experiment, initiate and implement new ideas by applying our know-how;
We are open with our managers, we raise and solve problems together, we improve our operations, and we celebrate victories together;
We are a young, ambitious, fast-growing company where you will always have exciting challenges and the taste of victory.
